Bear in mind this is an early character who has hit a lucky find, you
don't need to build a full ascension kit right now. 7 wishes is more
than enough to give you a major headstart, especially if you avoid
levelling up too quickly, and the rest of the items you want will turn
up sooner or later. In your position, my priorities for wishes would
be: ?ocharging, AC, HP, poison resist (if you don't already have it),
means of dealing with shopkeep and watch. Anything above that is just
gravy.

How about this: 2xB?oC, 2xB!oFH, SDSM, CoMR, tin of geen dragon meat
(if not already resistant), blessed fixed wand of death (I know
there's no point 'proofing it but hey...), speed boots. That gives you
a big stack of AC, a nice HP boost, reflection, magic resistance
speed, poison resistance. That's more than enough to take on the watch
if you're careful, or you could use the speed to just flee the level
and come back later.

It also leaves you one or two wishes to play with (depending on the
dragon tin) which could go on any of the following: Artifact weapon
(handy for killing watch), "oLS (YASD-proofing is never a bad thing,
particularly after a lucky find like this), 2xC?oG (for more HP later)
2x!oGA (a stat boost can be a big help to early characters) 2xC!oGL
(for a foolproof method of skipping out on the bill and avoiding the
watch- this would negate the need for a /oD), a =oRegeneration (if you
have plenty of food, and aren't happy with the HP from the potions)

Magic markers are great, but it's early in the game yet. You'll have
plenty of AC after your wishfest so there's no desperate need to be
writing scrolls until you find a marker randomly or get the castle
wand.

Archon-figurines don't have a 100% chance of being tame, so that could
be a wish wasted. You also don't want them turning on such a low-level
character.

Don't worry about having a 'spare wish'. How many spare wishes would a
normal character have at this stage of the game? Besides, Izchak might
have a surprise for you yet=-)



